In narrow form: policy and customer fields plus a small approved fact base, not a full company brain.

Field experiments show specific context beats generic:
- goal-specific reminders +16% saving, while generic reminders did nothing;
- a loan officer's name helped only repeat clients;
- a human two-way call raised on-time repayment by 34.4 pp LATE [l4cv].

No study tests AI voice with CRM context [l4c].

H8's kill condition (buyers want a point tool that plugs into what they have) is met on desk evidence:
- no buyer was found switching CRM for voice AI;
- point-first adoption: Zoho One is ~5% of Zoho's 1M+ paying customers;
- incumbents bundle voice [l4c, l4cv].

It is an expansion path. Revisit if 5 or more of the first 15 qualified prospects would buy voice only inside a replacement CRM [l4c].
